// Fixture (stdlib-namespace decompose-phase premise, PRD §0/§1 probe): `reify
// check` must emit `structure 'Mode' has no member 'eigenvalue'`.
//
// The OBSERVABLE is unchanged by task 5496's rename; the REASON it holds is
// not. Pre-rename this was the silent-collision defect: two stdlib modules both
// declared `structure def Mode`, and the two phases disagreed about the winner
// — compile-side template resolution took LAST-wins (std.modal.analysis) while
// the eval-side instantiation registry took FIRST-wins (std.solver.buckling).
// So buckling's `eigenvalue` was unreachable from user code even though a
// `Mode()` instance materialized at eval time carrying exactly that field.
//
// Post-rename the same diagnostic is simply correct, not a symptom: `Mode`
// unambiguously denotes std.modal.analysis's eigenpair
// (frequency/shape/participation_mass/damping_ratio), which genuinely has no
// `eigenvalue`. Buckling's eigenpair is now `BucklingMode`, and
// tests/prd-gate/fixtures/stdlib_ns_buckling_mode_coexist.ri pins that both are
// reachable from one file. The stdlib is kept collision-free by NS-P2's
// stdlib-build-time Error (crates/reify-compiler/src/stdlib_loader.rs).

structure def ModeMemberProbe {
    sub m = Mode()
    let e = m.eigenvalue
}
